  "conseguirCredencialesTexto": "It only takes once, it's free and no card is needed. You need the Google account that holds your sheets and your Drive, and about 10 minutes.",
  "verManualCapturas": "View the manual with screenshots",
  "guiaPaso1Titulo": "Create a project",
  "guiaPaso1Texto": "Sign in to Google Cloud Console with your Google account. At the top, press the project selector → \"New project\". Name: \"PitWall Control\". Press \"Create\" and check that it stays selected.",
  "abrirCloudConsole": "Open Cloud Console",
  "guiaPaso2Titulo": "Enable both APIs",
  "guiaPaso2Texto": "Enable \"Google Sheets API\" and also \"Google Drive API\" (press \"Enable\" on each). Otherwise the connection will fail.",
  "apiSheets": "Sheets API",
  "apiDrive": "Drive API",
  "pantallaDeConsentimiento": "Consent screen",
  "guiaPaso3Texto": "In \"Google Auth Platform\" press \"Get started\" and follow the wizard: 1) name \"PitWall Control\" and your support email; 2) Audience: choose \"External users\" (\"Internal\" only works for company accounts); 3) your contact email; 4) accept the data policy, \"Continue\" and \"Create\".",
  "guiaPaso4Titulo": "Add your account as a test user",
  "guiaPaso4Texto": "In the side menu go to \"Audience\" → \"Test users\" → \"Add users\". Type the Google email you will use to connect Control (and anyone else who will connect) and save. Without this step Google returns \"Error 403: access_denied\".",
  "publico": "Audience",
  "guiaPaso5Titulo": "Create the OAuth client",
  "guiaPaso5Texto": "In \"Clients\" press \"Create client\". Type: \"Desktop app\". Name: \"PitWall Control Desktop\". Press \"Create\".",
  "clientes": "Clients",
  "guiaPaso6Titulo": "Copy the ID and the secret",
  "guiaPaso6Texto": "The client ID (ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com) and the secret appear. Copy them and press \"Download JSON\": Google only shows the secret at this moment. Paste them on the previous screen, press \"Save credentials\" and then \"Connect with Google\".",
  "guiaPaso7Titulo": "Authorise in the browser",
  "guiaPaso7Texto": "Choose the account from step 4. If \"Google hasn't verified this app\" appears, press \"Advanced\" → \"Go to PitWall Control (unsafe)\", tick all the permissions and \"Continue\".",
  "avisoPrueba7Dias": "So it doesn't expire after 7 days: while the app is in \"Testing\" status, Google signs you out every 7 days. In \"Audience\" press \"Publish app\" (it moves to \"In production\"); for personal use it needs no verification.",
  "cosasQueSuelenFallar": "Things that often fail:",
